easures.\n\nLet's produce output.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? Not specified. Probably simple lines.\n\nReturn rating of this proposal, echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\".\n\nLet's output as:\n\nid: P2473\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 3\netc.\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nMake sure evidence is one sentence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nOriginality_evidence: The proposal applies sketching and compressed sensing to AI model logging, which is an unusual technical combination for regulatory traceability. Score 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness_evidence: It explicitly reframes mandatory logging as a scientific transparency research agenda, weaving compliance into R&D rather than treating it as separate overhead. Score 3.\n\nEffectiveness_evidence: If successful, efficient observability would reduce cost of compliant logging, but as a research investigation it only contributes to rather than guarantees a solution to the mandate. Score 3.\n\nApplicability_evidence: Reducing computational and storage overhead for event logs directly addresses the Article 12 requirement for automatic recording over the system lifetime. Score 4.\n\nAcceptability_evidence: Developing more efficient logging methods raises no legal, social or political concerns and aligns with EU transparency goals. Score 4.\n\nImplementability_evidence: Running experiments on sketching algorithms and benchmarking against standard logging requires dedicated researcher time and infrastructure but is a reasonably feasible research effort. Score 3.\n\nCheck levels.\n\nPotentially paradigm_relatedness could be 2? Slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Hmm it says transforms regulatory constraint into scientific contribution. That's more than slightly. I'd keep 3