learly applies to stated problem. Anchor 4 solves identified problem directly related; 3 solves implied problem related; 2 may have some benefit within special situation... Proposal is about privacy-preserving logs, which relates to logging mandate but is about future technique not immediate compliance. Maybe 3 solves implied problem related (privacy tension). Could be 2. I'd argue it addresses an implied concern about privacy in logging. So applicability 3.\n\nEvidence: The study targets log content sensitivity, an implied risk linked to mandatory event recording under Article 12.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree idea preserves or modifies paradigm. Anchors: 4 paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. 3 paradigm stretching changes that relationship e.g., logging woven into science, new partners... 2 slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 paradigm preserving standard compliance.\n\nResearch on privacy-preserving forensic logging introduces new elements and could change relationship between R&D and compliance? It makes compliance a research topic. Might be paradigm stretching? The description: advances knowledge frontier of AI safety by balancing transparency requirements with strict data privacy. That sounds like changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations -> paradigm stretching? Anchor 3 = changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into the science, new partners or offerings born from compliance). Could be 3.\n\nOr 4 = introduces new elements AND changes relationship ... or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. It does address larger problem? Maybe not. I'd say 3.\n\nEvidence: The proposal reframes mandatory logging as a scientific research problem rather than an operational compliance task.\n\nOriginality: degree rare and ingenious. Anchor 4 not expressed before AND ingenious imaginative surprising; 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination; 2 interesting; 1 common mundane boring.\n\nPrivacy-preserving forensic logging with MPC/differential privacy is unusual interesting but not completely novel? Might be 3. Could be 2 interesting. I'd say 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination.\n\nEvidence: Combining secure multi-party computation and differential privacy for forensic AI logs is an unusual approach within typical compliance responses.\n\nReturn JSON with id and fields.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence first then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably output as lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1452\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 2\netc.\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nProceed.",
